.TH MYSTRNCPY 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrncpy \- copy at most n characters and terminate the result
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <mystrfunctions.h>

int mystrncpy(char *dest, const char *src, int n);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrncpy
copies at most
.I n
characters from
.I src
to
.IR dest .
It always writes a terminating null byte after the copied characters.
The destination therefore needs room for at least
.I n + 1
bytes when the source is long enough. Unlike the standard C
.BR strncpy (3),
this function does not pad unused space with null bytes. Source and
destination must not overlap.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters copied, excluding the terminator.
Returns -1 if a pointer is NULL or
.I n
is negative.
